      {
        "id": "p29-cc-1-3-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "The expansion for $\\cos(2x)=2\\cos^2x+1$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False. $\\cos(2x)=2\\cos^2x-1$.",
          "worked": "False. The cosine double-angle identity is $\\cos(2x)=2\\cos^2x-1$, so the constant term is $-1$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p29-cc-1-3-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "The maximum value of $\\sin x\\cos x$ is 1.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False. The maximum is $\\frac12$.",
          "worked": "False. Using the sine double-angle identity,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin x\\cos x&=\\frac12\\sin 2x.\\end{align*}$$\nSince the maximum value of $\\sin 2x$ is 1, the maximum value of the product is $\\frac12$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p29-cc-1-3-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p29-cc-1-3-c-clarified-statement",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "If ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "\\tan 2x",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " is defined, then ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "\\tan x",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " must also be defined.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False. For $x=90^\\circ$, $\\tan 2x=0$, but $\\tan x$ is undefined.",
          "worked": "False. Take $x=90^\\circ$. Then $\\tan 2x=\\tan 180^\\circ=0$ is defined, while $\\tan x=\\tan 90^\\circ$ is undefined.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      }
    ]
